<a2ui>
$/={comparison_data:[{factor:"Curriculum",cbse:"Built around NCERT and a structured, concept-based syllabus; it is widely aligned with Indian competitive exams such as JEE, NEET, and CUET.[1][3]",cisce:"A broader, more content-rich syllabus with strong language depth and separate treatment of subjects such as History/Civics and Geography from middle school onward.",ib:"Inquiry-based, concept-led, and interdisciplinary, with programmes such as MYP and DP designed around global-minded learning."},{factor:"Assessment",cbse:"More exam-led, with longer papers and many question types covering recall, understanding, application, and evaluation.",cisce:"Exam-heavy but typically more descriptive and detailed, with required external assessment and internal components.[5]",ib:"Uses a mix of internal and external assessment; MYP external assessment is optional, and DP adds essays, projects, and other coursework-heavy elements.[7]"},{factor:"Subject flexibility",cbse:"Generally more structured with fewer combinations than international curricula.[13]",cisce:"Moderate flexibility, but still more fixed than IB.",ib:"Greater flexibility, especially in subject choice and in how learners connect disciplines."},{factor:"Transferability",cbse:"Transfers most cleanly between CBSE schools within India; CBSE also has the broadest domestic footprint.[8][11]",cisce:"Transfers best within CISCE schools, but the smaller school network can make moves less convenient than CBSE.",ib:"Best when moving between international schools; recognition is global, but local transfer can depend on school level and subject mapping."}]}
root=Column([a,b,c,g,k,q],gap="md",padding=16)
a=Text("Quick comparison","h2")
b=Table(columns=[{key:"factor",label:"Factor"},{key:"cbse",label:"CBSE"},{key:"cisce",label:"CISCE"},{key:"ib",label:"IB"}],statePath="/comparison_data",domain="comparison",preferredPresentation="table")
c=Card([d])
d=Column([e,f,g],"sm",padding=16)
e=Text("What each board suits best","h3")
f=Text("CBSE works well for families prioritizing a clear syllabus, frequent school availability, and a strong fit with Indian entrance-exam preparation.",variant="body")
g=Column([h,i,j],"sm")
h=Text("CISCE suits students who want more depth, stronger English exposure, and a broader academic experience across sciences, humanities, and languages.",variant="body")
i=Text("IB suits students who thrive on discussion, projects, research, and a less exam-dominant approach, especially if the family values global mobility.",variant="body")
j=Text("This comparison is based on general educational philosophies and should not replace personalized guidance from your school.",variant="body")
k=Card([l])
l=Column([m,n],"sm",padding=16)
m=Text("Questions to ask prospective schools","h3")
n=Column([o,p,q,r,s,t,u],"sm")
o=Text("Which programme do you actually offer at secondary level: CBSE, ICSE/ISC, or IB MYP/DP?",variant="body")
p=Text("How many subject combinations are available in Classes 9–10 and 11–12, and can students change them later?",variant="body")
q=Text("What proportion of marks comes from board exams, internal assessment, projects, practicals, and coursework?",variant="body")
r=Text("How do you support students who may transfer to another school or board in the future?",variant="body")
s=Text("For IB schools, which subjects are offered in the school, and how do they align with university goals?",variant="body")
t=Text("For CBSE or CISCE schools, how do you balance board preparation with deeper learning and stress management?",variant="body")
u=Text("What are the class sizes, teacher qualifications, lab resources, and language support for the secondary years?",variant="body")
v=Text("Current fee, seat-availability, and school-specific transfer data were not consistently available across the sources, so families should verify these directly with each school.",variant="body")
</a2ui>